==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[CTO Seal]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Spacefish Jones]] spawns as the boss after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Dogenstein]]s spawn after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*5 [[Doctor K.O.]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[CTO Seal]] spawns after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Due to CTO Seal having 100% freeze uptime you'll either need [[:Category:Cats with Freeze Immunity|units with Immune to Freeze]] to win or some way to outrange them. [[Li'l Tank Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Eraser Cat]]'s Freeze Immunity, combined with [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] and [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]], are enough to stall the enemies in this stage. [[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Carpenter Cat]] with his Sage Slayer, freeze immunity, & resistant to Red/Floating counters every enemy in this stage save for Kroxo, making him a prime pick here. Quickly deal with Doctor K.O with [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], which will gradually chip CTO Seal down. [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]], [[Urs & Fenrir (Special Cat)|Awakened Urs]] and [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] are good options for dealing with CTO Seal.

